      "extract": "A two-variable link invariant – the HOMFLY-PT polynomial – can be recovered using a family of trace functions on Iwahori–Hecke algebras in type A satisfying analogues of the conditions in Markov’s the- orem for the braid group (usually called ‘Markov moves’) [10]. The analogues of Markov moves can be formulated for Iwahori–Hecke algebras of other Coxeter groups, leading to a general notion of the Markov trace, see,",
